                <pb facs="0750" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg680"/>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram from <placeName>Vera Cruz</placeName> to
                        Mexico. Received in Mexico <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-08-26">the
                            26th August, 1867</date>, at 7. 29 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">To the Citizen Minister of War:</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The Austrian Admiral Tegethoff arrived at Sacrificios this morning in the
                    Elizabeth, a war steamer of his nation.</p>
                <p>He sent a message to this military command, asking permission to proceed to the
                    capital to solicit the body of Maximilian from the supreme government, for the
                    purpose of taking it away. I desire to know if he may be permitted to go to the
                    city of Mexico.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ZEREGA.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
